    <main class="window active is-bright">
      <div class="title-bar">
        <div class="title-bar-text">x.css</div>
        <div class="title-bar-controls">
          <button aria-label="Close"></button>
          <button aria-label="Minimize"></button>
          <button aria-label="Maximize"></button>
          <button aria-label="Fullscreen"></button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="window-body has-space">
        <h1 class="header header-document center">x.css</h1>
        <p class="desc center">A design system for building Mac OS X Lion interfaces</p>

        <h2 id="intro">Intro</h2>
        <p>x.css is a CSS library for building interfaces that look like Mac OS X Lion (10.7, 2011): aqua buttons, glossy traffic lights, gradient title bars and blue source-list selections.</p>
        <p>It shares its markup API with <a href="https://github.com/khang-nd/7.css" target="_blank">7.css</a>, 98.css, XP.css and system.css: the same HTML renders as Lion here. It uses no JavaScript and works with any front-end framework.</p>

        <h2 id="install">Installation</h2>
        <pre><code>npm install @vstyler96/x.css</code></pre>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Use it when</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>dist/x.css</code></td><td>Styles everything; CSS variables (<code>--osx-*</code>) stay live for theming.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>dist/x.scoped.css</code></td><td>Styles only what is inside an element with <code>class="osx"</code>.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>dist/x.inline.css</code></td><td>Variables resolved, for old browsers.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>dist/gui/&lt;component&gt;.css</code></td><td>You want just one component.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2>Components</h2>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="balloon">Balloon</h3>
          <p>A popover with a tail. Use <code>role="tooltip"</code>. The tail sits top-left by default; move it with <code>.is-top</code> (tail at the bottom) and <code>.is-left</code> (tail on the right).</p>
          <%- example(`
            <div role="tooltip">A balloon, Lion style.</div>
            <br>
            <div role="tooltip" class="is-top is-left">The tail is at the bottom right.</div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="button">Button</h3>
          <blockquote>
            A push button is a rounded rectangle containing text. Clicking a push button performs the action described by its name.
            <footer>&mdash; Apple Human Interface Guidelines</footer>
          </blockquote>
          <p>Every <code>button</code> is a push button, at least 59px wide and 21px tall.</p>
          <%- example(`<button>Cancel</button> <button>Submit</button>`) %>
          <p>Pressed buttons turn aqua. Simulate it with <code>.active</code>; simulate focus with <code>.focused</code>.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <button[[ class="active"]]>Active</button>
            <button[[ class="focused"]]>Focused</button>
          `) %>
          <p>The default button pulses in aqua.</p>
          <%- example(`<button>Cancel</button> <button class="default">Find</button>`) %>
          <%- example(`<button disabled>Disabled</button>`) %>
          <p>The file input button and <code>label[role="button"]</code> get the same look.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <input type="file" />
            <label role="button" tabindex="0"><input type="file" /> Choose file…</label>
          `) %>
          <p>Lion's toolbar and list-bar styles are modifiers: <code>.is-textured</code> and <code>.is-gradient</code>.</p>
          <%- example(`<button class="is-textured">Textured</button> <button class="is-gradient">+</button>`) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="checkbox">Checkbox</h3>
          <%- example(`
            <div class="field-row">
              <input type="checkbox" id="cb${getNewId()}" checked>
              <label for="cb${getCurrentId()}">Show hidden files</label>
            </div>
            <div class="field-row">
              <input type="checkbox" id="cb${getNewId()}">
              <label for="cb${getCurrentId()}">Show item info</label>
            </div>
            <div class="field-row">
              <input type="checkbox" id="cb${getNewId()}" disabled>
              <label for="cb${getCurrentId()}">Disabled</label>
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="collapse">Collapse</h3>
          <p>A <code>details</code> element gets a disclosure triangle.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <details>
              <summary>More info</summary>
              <p>Kind: Application. Size: 4.2 MB.</p>
            </details>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="combobox">Combobox</h3>
          <%- example(`
            <div class="combobox" style="width: 12rem">
              <input type="text" aria-label="Font size" value="12" list="sizes">
              <button aria-label="Show sizes"></button>
              <datalist id="sizes"><option>9</option><option>12</option><option>18</option></datalist>
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="dropdown">Dropdown</h3>
          <p>A <code>select</code> is a Lion pop-up button: a push button with up/down arrows.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <select>
              <option>Name</option>
              <option>Date Modified</option>
              <option>Size</option>
            </select>
            <select disabled><option>Disabled</option></select>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="groupbox">GroupBox</h3>
          <p>Use <code>fieldset</code> and <code>legend</code>. Lay out controls with <code>.field-row</code> or <code>.field-row-stacked</code>.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <fieldset>
              <legend>Startup</legend>
              <div class="field-row">
                <input type="radio" id="rd${getNewId()}" name="gb" checked>
                <label for="rd${getCurrentId()}">Open new windows</label>
              </div>
              <div class="field-row">
                <input type="radio" id="rd${getNewId()}" name="gb">
                <label for="rd${getCurrentId()}">Reopen windows</label>
              </div>
              <div class="field-row-stacked" style="width: 200px">
                <label for="tx${getNewId()}">Home folder</label>
                <input type="text" id="tx${getCurrentId()}" value="/Users/vincent">
              </div>
            </fieldset>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="listbox">ListBox</h3>
          <p>Use <code>role="listbox"</code> with <code>role="option"</code> children, or a <code>select multiple</code>. Mark the selection with <code>aria-selected="true"</code>. Add <code>.has-hover</code> or <code>.has-shadow</code> if you need them.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <ul role="listbox" class="has-hover" style="width: 200px">
              <li role="option">Desktop</li>
              <li role="option" aria-selected="true">Documents</li>
              <li role="option">Downloads</li>
              <li role="option">Movies</li>
            </ul>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="listview">ListView</h3>
          <p>A <code>table</code> looks like Finder's list view. <code>th.highlighted</code> marks the sorted column, and <code>.indicator</code> / <code>.indicator.up</code> add the sort arrow. <code>.is-striped</code> adds zebra rows, <code>.has-hover</code> highlights the row under the pointer, <code>.is-full</code> makes the table full width, and <code>.is-center</code> on a cell centres it. A <code>tr.highlighted</code> selection always wins over stripes and hover.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <table class="has-shadow is-striped has-hover is-full">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th class="highlighted indicator">Name</th>
                  <th>Date Modified</th>
                  <th class="is-center">Size</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Applications</td><td>Today, 9:41</td><td class="is-center">--</td></tr>
                <tr class="highlighted"><td>Documents</td><td>Yesterday</td><td class="is-center">--</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Notes.rtf</td><td>20 Jul 2011</td><td class="is-center">4 KB</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Photo.jpg</td><td>20 Jul 2011</td><td class="is-center">2.1 MB</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="menu">Menu &amp; MenuBar</h3>
          <p>Use <code>ul[role="menubar"]</code> &gt; <code>li[role="menuitem"]</code> &gt; <code>ul[role="menu"]</code>. Menus open on focus; add <code>.can-hover</code> to open them on hover too. <code>.has-divider</code> adds a separator, and <code>aria-disabled</code> greys an item out. <code>.is-apple</code> is the Apple menu.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <ul role="menubar" class="can-hover">
              <li role="menuitem" tabindex="0" aria-haspopup="true" class="is-apple">Apple
                <ul role="menu">
                  <li role="menuitem" class="has-divider"><a href="#menu">About This Mac</a></li>
                  <li role="menuitem"><a href="#menu">System Preferences…</a></li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li role="menuitem" tabindex="0" aria-haspopup="true">File
                <ul role="menu">
                  <li role="menuitem"><a href="#menu">New Window</a></li>
                  <li role="menuitem" class="has-divider"><a href="#menu">Open…</a></li>
                  <li role="menuitem" aria-haspopup="true" tabindex="0">Open Recent
                    <ul role="menu">
                      <li role="menuitem"><a href="#menu">Notes.rtf</a></li>
                      <li role="menuitem"><a href="#menu">Photo.jpg</a></li>
                    </ul>
                  </li>
                  <li role="menuitem" aria-disabled="true"><a href="#menu">Print…</a></li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li role="menuitem" tabindex="0" aria-haspopup="true">View
                <ul role="menu">
                  <li role="menuitem"><input type="radio" name="mnv" id="mn${getNewId()}" checked><label for="mn${getCurrentId()}">as Icons</label></li>
                  <li role="menuitem" class="has-divider"><input type="radio" name="mnv" id="mn${getNewId()}"><label for="mn${getCurrentId()}">as List</label></li>
                  <li role="menuitem"><input type="checkbox" id="mn${getNewId()}" checked><label for="mn${getCurrentId()}">Show Toolbar</label></li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li role="menuitem" tabindex="0" aria-haspopup="false"><a href="#menu">Help</a></li>
            </ul>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="progressbar">ProgressBar</h3>
          <p>Use <code>role="progressbar"</code> with an inner <code>div</code> whose width is the value. <code>.animate</code> adds moving stripes, <code>.paused</code> turns it graphite and <code>.error</code> red. <code>.marquee</code> is the indeterminate Aqua barber pole.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <div role="progressbar" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-valuenow="60"><div style="width: 60%"></div></div>
            <div role="progressbar" class="animate"><div style="width: 40%"></div></div>
            <div role="progressbar" class="paused"><div style="width: 50%"></div></div>
            <div role="progressbar" class="error"><div style="width: 30%"></div></div>
            <div role="progressbar" class="marquee"></div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="radiobutton">Radio Button</h3>
          <%- example(`
            <div class="field-row">
              <input type="radio" id="rd${getNewId()}" name="rd-ex" checked>
              <label for="rd${getCurrentId()}">Left</label>
            </div>
            <div class="field-row">
              <input type="radio" id="rd${getNewId()}" name="rd-ex">
              <label for="rd${getCurrentId()}">Right</label>
            </div>
            <div class="field-row">
              <input type="radio" id="rd${getNewId()}" name="rd-ex" disabled>
              <label for="rd${getCurrentId()}">Disabled</label>
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="scrollbar">Scrollbar</h3>
          <p>Lion's thin, rounded scrollbars are opt-in: add <code>.has-scrollbar</code> to the scrolling element.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <div class="has-scrollbar" style="width: 240px; height: 80px; overflow: auto; background: #fff">
              <div style="width: 400px; height: 200px; padding: 8px">Scroll me in both directions.</div>
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="searchbox">SearchBox</h3>
          <%- example(`
            <input type="search" placeholder="Search" aria-label="Search">
            <div class="searchbox">
              <input type="search" placeholder="Spotlight" aria-label="Spotlight">
              <button aria-label="search"></button>
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="slider">Slider</h3>
          <p>Use <code>input type="range"</code>. <code>.has-box-indicator</code> gives the pointed knob used with tick marks. Wrap the input in <code>.is-vertical</code> to make it vertical.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <div class="field-row" style="width: 300px">
              <label>Slow</label><input type="range" min="0" max="10" value="4" aria-label="Speed"><label>Fast</label>
            </div>
            <div class="field-row" style="width: 300px">
              <input type="range" class="has-box-indicator" min="0" max="10" value="6" aria-label="Size">
            </div>
            <div class="is-vertical">
              <input type="range" min="0" max="10" value="3" aria-label="Volume">
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="spinner">Spinner</h3>
          <p>The asynchronous progress indicator. Add <code>.animate</code> to make it spin.</p>
          <%- example(`<span class="spinner" aria-label="Loading"></span> <span class="spinner animate" aria-label="Loading"></span>`) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="tabs">Tabs</h3>
          <p>Lion tabs are a centred segmented control over a sunken panel. Use <code>menu[role="tablist"]</code> with <code>button[role="tab"]</code>, and mark the current tab with <code>aria-selected="true"</code>. <code>.justified</code> stretches the tabs across the panel.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <section class="tabs" style="max-width: 500px">
              <menu role="tablist" aria-label="Preferences">
                <button role="tab" aria-controls="tab-general" aria-selected="true">General</button>
                <button role="tab" aria-controls="tab-labels">Labels</button>
                <button role="tab" aria-controls="tab-advanced">Advanced</button>
                <button role="tab" aria-controls="tab-x" disabled>Disabled</button>
              </menu>
              <article role="tabpanel" id="tab-general">Show these items on the desktop.</article>
              <article role="tabpanel" id="tab-labels" hidden>Use these label names.</article>
              <article role="tabpanel" id="tab-advanced" hidden>Show all filename extensions.</article>
            </section>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="textbox">TextBox</h3>
          <%- example(`
            <div class="field-row-stacked" style="width: 220px">
              <label for="tx${getNewId()}">Email</label>
              <input id="tx${getCurrentId()}" type="email" placeholder="steve@apple.com">
              <label for="tx${getNewId()}">Password</label>
              <input id="tx${getCurrentId()}" type="password" value="password">
              <label for="tx${getNewId()}">Comments</label>
              <textarea id="tx${getCurrentId()}" rows="3"></textarea>
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="treeview">TreeView</h3>
          <p>Use <code>ul.tree-view</code> with nested <code>details</code>. <code>.has-container</code> adds a white box, <code>.has-collapse-button</code> hangs the triangles in the gutter, and <code>.has-connector</code> draws guide lines.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <ul class="tree-view has-container has-collapse-button" style="width: 240px">
              <li>Macintosh HD</li>
              <li>
                <details open>
                  <summary>Users</summary>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Shared</li>
                    <li>
                      <details>
                        <summary>vincent</summary>
                        <ul><li>Desktop</li><li>Documents</li></ul>
                      </details>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </details>
              </li>
              <li>Applications</li>
            </ul>
          `) %>
          <%- example(`
            <ul class="tree-view has-connector" style="width: 240px">
              <li>Library
                <ul><li>Fonts</li><li>Preferences</li></ul>
              </li>
            </ul>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="typography">Typography</h3>
          <%- example(`
            <h2 class="header header-document">Document header</h2>
            <h3 class="header header-group">Group header</h3>
            <p class="instruction instruction-primary">Do you want to save the changes?</p>
            <p class="instruction">Your changes will be lost if you don't save them.</p>
            <a href="#typography">A link</a>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <h2>Window</h2>
        <blockquote>
          Windows have standard parts: a title bar with close, minimize and zoom buttons on the left, and the full screen button on the right.
          <footer>&mdash; Apple Human Interface Guidelines</footer>
        </blockquote>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="title-bar">Title Bar</h3>
          <p>The markup is the same as 7.css: <code>.title-bar-text</code> and <code>.title-bar-controls</code>. Identify buttons by <code>aria-label</code> (<code>Close</code>, <code>Minimize</code>, <code>Maximize</code>, <code>Restore</code>, <code>Help</code>, <code>Fullscreen</code>) or by class (<code>.is-close</code> and so on). Whatever the order in the HTML, the traffic lights go on the left, and Help and Fullscreen go on the right.</p>
          <p>A title bar is inactive (grey) unless it or its window has <code>.active</code>. The glyphs appear when you hover the bar.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <div class="window active">
              <div class="title-bar">
                <div class="title-bar-text">An active title bar</div>
                <div class="title-bar-controls">
                  <button aria-label="Minimize"></button>
                  <button aria-label="Maximize"></button>
                  <button aria-label="Close"></button>
                  <button aria-label="Fullscreen"></button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <br>
            <div class="window">
              <div class="title-bar">
                <div class="title-bar-text">An inactive title bar</div>
                <div class="title-bar-controls">
                  <button aria-label="Close"></button>
                  <button aria-label="Minimize"></button>
                  <button aria-label="Maximize"></button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <br>
            <div class="window active">
              <div class="title-bar">
                <div class="title-bar-text">With help, by class</div>
                <div class="title-bar-controls">
                  <button class="is-close" aria-label="Close window"></button>
                  <button class="is-minimize" disabled aria-label="Minimize window"></button>
                  <button class="is-restore" aria-label="Zoom"></button>
                  <button class="is-help" aria-label="Show help"></button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="window-contents">Window Contents</h3>
          <p>Put content in <code>.window-body</code>. <code>.has-space</code> adds padding, <code>.has-scrollbar</code> gives Lion scrollbars, and <code>.is-bright</code> on the window makes the body white. <code>.status-bar</code> &gt; <code>.status-bar-field</code> and <code>.window-footer</code> (or a <code>footer</code>) sit at the bottom.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <div class="window active" style="width: 360px">
              <div class="title-bar">
                <div class="title-bar-text">Macintosh HD</div>
                <div class="title-bar-controls">
                  <button aria-label="Close"></button>
                  <button aria-label="Minimize"></button>
                  <button aria-label="Maximize"></button>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="window-body has-space has-scrollbar" style="height: 80px">
                Woo, I got stuff in me!
              </div>
              <div class="status-bar">
                <p class="status-bar-field">4 items</p>
                <p class="status-bar-field">212 GB available</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <br>
            <div class="window active is-bright" style="width: 360px">
              <div class="title-bar">
                <div class="title-bar-text">Accounts</div>
                <div class="title-bar-controls"><button aria-label="Close"></button></div>
              </div>
              <div class="window-body has-space">A bright window body.</div>
              <div class="window-footer">
                <button class="is-gradient">+</button>
                <button class="is-gradient">&minus;</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="dialog">Dialog &amp; Sheet</h3>
          <p>A dialog is <code>.window[role="dialog"]</code>. As in 7.css, it is hidden until its <code>id</code> is the URL fragment, so a link opens it without JavaScript. Add <code>.is-sheet</code> to get a Lion sheet that drops from the top of the screen, with a flat top and rounded bottom.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <a href="#dialog-demo">Open dialog</a> &middot; <a href="#sheet-demo">Open sheet</a>

            <div class="window active" id="dialog-demo" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="dialog-title" style="width: 320px">
              <div class="title-bar">
                <div class="title-bar-text" id="dialog-title">Copy</div>
                <div class="title-bar-controls">
                  <button aria-label="Close" onclick="history.back()"></button>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="window-body has-space">
                <p class="instruction">Copying 12 items to “Backup”</p>
                <div role="progressbar" class="marquee"></div>
              </div>
              <footer style="justify-content: flex-end">
                <button onclick="history.back()">Stop</button>
              </footer>
            </div>

            <div class="window active is-sheet" id="sheet-demo" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="sheet-title" style="width: 420px">
              <div class="window-body has-space">
                <p class="instruction instruction-primary" id="sheet-title">Do you want to save the changes made to “Notes”?</p>
                <p class="instruction">Your changes will be lost if you don't save them.</p>
                <div class="field-row" style="justify-content: flex-end">
                  <button onclick="history.back()">Don't Save</button>
                  <button onclick="history.back()">Cancel</button>
                  <button class="default" onclick="history.back()">Save</button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <h2 id="extras">Extras</h2>
        <p>These are Lion-only components. They follow the same rules as the rest: ARIA roles, <code>.is-*</code> / <code>.has-*</code> modifiers and <code>--osx-*</code> variables.</p>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="toolbar">Toolbar</h3>
          <p>A <code>.toolbar</code> right after <code>.title-bar</code> merges with it into Lion's unified title bar. <code>.is-spacer</code> adds a fixed gap and <code>.is-flexible</code> takes up the remaining space.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <div class="window active" style="width: 480px">
              <div class="title-bar">
                <div class="title-bar-text">Finder</div>
                <div class="title-bar-controls">
                  <button aria-label="Close"></button>
                  <button aria-label="Minimize"></button>
                  <button aria-label="Maximize"></button>
                  <button aria-label="Fullscreen"></button>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="toolbar">
                <div class="segmented is-textured">
                  <button aria-label="Back">&#9664;</button>
                  <button aria-label="Forward">&#9654;</button>
                </div>
                <span class="is-flexible"></span>
                <input type="search" placeholder="Search" aria-label="Search">
              </div>
              <div class="window-body has-space">Content</div>
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="segmented">Segmented Control</h3>
          <p>Put <code>input</code> + <code>label</code> pairs, or plain <code>button</code>s with <code>aria-pressed</code>, inside <code>.segmented</code>. <code>.is-textured</code> gives the toolbar style, and <code>.is-gradient</code> gives the add/remove bar used under lists.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <div class="segmented">
              <input type="radio" name="seg" id="seg${getNewId()}" checked><label for="seg${getCurrentId()}">Desktop</label>
              <input type="radio" name="seg" id="seg${getNewId()}"><label for="seg${getCurrentId()}">Mobile</label>
              <input type="radio" name="seg" id="seg${getNewId()}"><label for="seg${getCurrentId()}">Web</label>
            </div>
            <br><br>
            <div class="segmented is-textured">
              <input type="radio" name="tex" id="tex${getNewId()}" checked><label for="tex${getCurrentId()}">Icons</label>
              <input type="radio" name="tex" id="tex${getNewId()}"><label for="tex${getCurrentId()}">List</label>
              <input type="radio" name="tex" id="tex${getNewId()}"><label for="tex${getCurrentId()}">Columns</label>
            </div>
            <br><br>
            <div class="segmented is-gradient" style="width: 12rem">
              <button aria-label="Add">+</button>
              <button aria-label="Remove">&minus;</button>
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="scope-bar">Scope Bar</h3>
          <p>A <code>.scope-bar</code> narrows a search. Radio + label pairs become pill buttons, and <code>button</code>, <code>select</code> and <code>input</code> get the small rounded style.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <div class="scope-bar">
              <span>Search:</span>
              <input type="radio" name="scope" id="sc${getNewId()}"><label for="sc${getCurrentId()}">This Mac</label>
              <input type="radio" name="scope" id="sc${getNewId()}" checked><label for="sc${getCurrentId()}">Documents</label>
              <select aria-label="Attribute"><option>Name</option><option>Kind</option></select>
              <button>Save</button>
              <button aria-label="Remove">&minus;</button>
              <button aria-label="Add">+</button>
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <section class="component">
          <h3 id="source-list">Source List</h3>
          <p>The blue sidebar from Finder and iTunes. Use <code>.splitview</code> &gt; <code>.sourcelist</code>. Each group is a <code>details</code> whose <code>summary</code> is the heading (hover it to see Show/Hide). Items are radio + label pairs. A nested <code>details</code> gets a disclosure triangle, and <code>.badge</code> and <code>.icon</code> decorate items.</p>
          <%- example(`
            <div class="window active">
              <div class="title-bar">
                <div class="title-bar-text">Library</div>
                <div class="title-bar-controls">
                  <button aria-label="Close"></button>
                  <button aria-label="Minimize"></button>
                  <button aria-label="Maximize"></button>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="splitview">
                <nav class="sourcelist">
                  <details open>
                    <summary>Library</summary>
                    <input type="radio" name="sl" id="sl${getNewId()}" checked><label for="sl${getCurrentId()}">Music</label>
                    <input type="radio" name="sl" id="sl${getNewId()}"><label for="sl${getCurrentId()}">Movies</label>
                    <input type="radio" name="sl" id="sl${getNewId()}"><label for="sl${getCurrentId()}">Podcasts <span class="badge">4</span></label>
                  </details>
                  <details open>
                    <summary>Lists</summary>
                    <details>
                      <summary>Fonts</summary>
                      <input type="radio" name="sl" id="sl${getNewId()}"><label for="sl${getCurrentId()}">Helvetica Neue</label>
                      <input type="radio" name="sl" id="sl${getNewId()}"><label for="sl${getCurrentId()}">Lucida Grande</label>
                    </details>
                  </details>
                </nav>
                <div class="window-body has-space is-bright" style="background: #fff">Hi, my name is Window.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          `) %>
        </section>

        <h2 id="contributing">Credits</h2>
        <p>x.css is maintained by <a href="https://github.com/vstyler96" target="_blank">Vincent GS</a>. It started as a fork of <a href="https://github.com/sakofchit/system.css" target="_blank">system.css</a> by Sakun Acharige. The Lion styles are ported from the Lion CSS UI Kit by <a href="http://foolproof.me" target="_blank">Ville V. Vanninen</a>, and the architecture follows <a href="https://github.com/khang-nd/7.css" target="_blank">7.css</a>. Bugs and PRs are welcome on <a href="https://github.com/vstyler96/x.css/issues">GitHub</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>

  <script>
    // tabs demo: switch panels on click
    document.querySelectorAll("menu[role=tablist]").forEach((list) => {
      list.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
        const tab = e.target.closest("[role=tab]");
        if (!tab || tab.disabled) return;
        list.querySelectorAll("[role=tab]").forEach((t) => {
          t.setAttribute("aria-selected", t === tab);
          document.getElementById(t.getAttribute("aria-controls"))?.toggleAttribute("hidden", t !== tab);
        });
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
